From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/log: keep the scanout when userspace has the screen first

drm_log sets up its scanout when its printing thread first runs.  On a
kernel without preemption on one CPU that is after init has started, and
a userspace display server may be DRM master by then: the commit failed,
the buffers were freed, and nothing was left for restore() to show when
the server let the screen go, which stayed dark.  The scanouts are now
kept whether the first commit succeeds or not; drawing already waits for
no master, and restore() commits them.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/clients/drm_log.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/clients/drm_log.c
@@ -272,7 +272,7 @@
 {
 	struct drm_client_dev *client = &dlog->client;
 	struct drm_mode_set *mode_set;
-	int i, max_modeset;
+	int max_modeset;
 	int n_modeset = 0;
 
 	dlog->probed = true;
@@ -300,16 +300,16 @@
 	if (n_modeset == 0)
 		goto err_nomodeset;
 
-	if (drm_client_modeset_commit(client))
-		goto err_failed_commit;
+	/*
+	 * Userspace may hold the screen already, when the printing thread
+	 * first runs after it started: the commit fails, and the scanouts are
+	 * kept for restore() to show once it lets the screen go.
+	 */
+	drm_client_modeset_commit(client);
 
 	dlog->n_scanout = n_modeset;
 	return;
 
-err_failed_commit:
-	for (i = 0; i < n_modeset; i++)
-		drm_client_buffer_delete(dlog->scanout[i].buffer);
-
 err_nomodeset:
 	kfree(dlog->scanout);
 	dlog->scanout = NULL;
